  "question": "Background / Context:\n\nSilk is a live profiling and inspection tool specifically designed for the Django framework. It serves as a performance analysis system by intercepting and storing HTTP requests and database queries. This allows developers to inspect and visualize runtime operations through a user interface, facilitating debugging and optimization.\n\nObjectives:\n\nThe primary objective of Silk is to provide real-time insights into the performance of Django applications. This includes profiling HTTP requests, responses, SQL queries, and code blocks, helping developers identify and resolve bottlenecks.\n\nStakeholders & Users:\n\n- Primary Users: Django developers needing real-time profiling and diagnostics.\n- Stakeholders: Development teams, Quality Assurance teams, Project Managers, and any entity involved in Django application performance optimization.\n\nFunctional Descriptions:\n\n1. Middleware Integration: Integrates as middleware to intercept and log HTTP requests and responses for profiling purposes.\n   \n2. SQL Query Profiling: Wraps around SQL execution to capture and profile database queries, allowing analysis of query performance.\n\n3. Code Profiling: Utilizes a context manager and decorator to enable profiling of specific code blocks or functions, giving developers flexibility in what to profile.\n\n4. User Interface: Provides a graphical user interface for inspecting and visualizing the captured data, including HTTP transactions and SQL queries.\n\n5. Data Relationships: Maintains data relationships, such as linking requests to their corresponding SQL queries, to provide comprehensive profiling context.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions:\n\n- Performance: The system should minimally impact the performance of the application being profiled to ensure accurate representations of typical operation scenarios.\n\n- Usability: The user interface should be intuitive, enabling quick access and understanding of the profiling data without requiring extensive training.\n\n- Scalability: Must efficiently handle large volumes of requests and queries, ensuring it remains effective in high-traffic environments.\n\n- Security: Ensures that sensitive data captured during profiling is securely handled, adhering to data protection standards.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0025\nCREATE TABLE `silk_request` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `method` varchar(16) NOT NULL,\n  `query_params` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  `body` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  `response_status_code` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `response_body` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `time_taken_ms` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `meta` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `silk_sqlquery` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `request_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `query` longtext NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `time_taken_ms` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `raw_sql` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  `params` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  `alias` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `is_slow` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `silk_sqlquery_request_id_idx` (`request_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `silk_sqlquery_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`request_id`) REFERENCES `silk_request` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `silk_profile` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `kind` varchar(32) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `time_taken_ms` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `silk_profile_stat` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `profile_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `count` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `time_taken_ms` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `average_time_ms` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `silk_profile_stat_profile_id_idx` (`profile_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `silk_profile_stat_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`profile_id`) REFERENCES `silk_profile` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
